  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Professionalisation of the horticulture sector Dalaba, Guinea</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of the requested study is to assess the possibilities to revitalise and rehabilitate the Centre de Promotion de l&#x2019;Horticulture (CPH) in Dalaba in order to improve the  horticultural production in Guinea, reinforce the capacity and knowledge of the CPH regarding production and promotion of horticultural products grown in the region specifically potatoes, and of improving food security in general. The assignment is set-up in two phases A and B respectively, with a go/no-go decision foreseen in between:Phase A consists of studies to analyse the horticultural sector, to determine what is necessary to rehabilitate and revitalise the CPH in terms of functionality and capacity, and to assess the financial, economic, institutional and environmental feasibility of the project.  This stage includes a preliminary Technical Design and Cost Assessment as well as an Environmental and Social Impact Assessment (ESIA).Phase B consists of the preparation of a tender dossier for selecting a contractor, which will rehabilitate and build the infrastructure of the CPH, deliver the required equipment and supply the required technical assistance. This will include drafting the overall specifications and design criteria  to enable the contractor to prepare the Detailed Design and cost estimates. As well as specifications on the Technical Assistance to be supplied. The output of phase B will be a complete tender package for a design and build project ready to be put in the market.</narrative>
  </description>
